// Ch4 C4-08 "Cutscene: the long way round" (docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch04.md). 05:30, the dawn low
// water (B11: "At first tide. The causeway won't wait for me."). The village is at the wall again,
// its lamps guttering in the first light. H08 (dawn grade): Asha stops at the wall and touches her
// shell. The ink on it and on her mother's is new and black and still glossy, always (the re-inking
// happens whether or not the player watched it). She looks at her fingertip. She doesn't know who did
// it. If ch04_saw_ysolde_ink, Rhen does, and a look is enough (no line).
// Neme: in Ch2 she never once looked at Asha's packed bag (B02). Now she looks at her the whole time,
// and says one thing.
// The causeway (C01, C02 at dawn): by custom nobody walks past the wall with the Cantor but her
// guardians. Toma leads, Asha in the middle, and Rhen walks behind, as Toma told him to in B11, without
// a word about it. Hold C01 long as the three get small (pillar 3). Nobody looks back except Rhen, once.
// Watch: not a dock farewell. Nobody waves a boat away; she walks out on her own feet.
// Music: haluna_dawn (reprise). The chapter flow then goes to ch04/brightwater_ferry at Landing.
title: ch04_long_way_round
location: ch04/haluna_wake
---
@letterbox on
@music haluna_dawn fade=3.0
@fade in 2.0
@camera H08 grade=ch02
@anim asha touch_shell
@wait 2.0
@anim asha look_at_fingertip
@wait 1.5
<<if $ch04_saw_ysolde_ink>>
@anim rhen look_away
@wait 1.2
<<endif>>
@anim neme watch asha
@wait 1.5
Neme [sad]: Eat when they feed you. #line:ch04_dawn_001
Asha [soft_smile]: I will. #line:ch04_dawn_002
@wait 1.0
@camera C01 grade=ch02
@mark toma causeway_toma walk via=wall_away,way_wall_east,way_rail_gap,way_flats
@mark asha causeway_asha walk via=wall_away,way_wall_east,way_rail_gap,way_flats
@mark rhen causeway_rhen walk
@wait 14.0
@anim rhen look_back
@wait 1.5
@camera C02 grade=ch02
@wait 18.0
@fade out 2.0
@letterbox off
===
